-- title:
--   Theorem 3, necessary and sufficient saturation criteria
-- statement:
--   Let $d\ge1$, $H=\mathbb C^{\mathbb Z_d}$, and $Z=\mathbb Z_d\times\mathbb Z_d$. In the specified orthonormal basis let $W_{(x,y)}=U^xV^y$, where $Ue_k=e_{k+1}$ and $Ve_k=e^{2\pi i k/d}e_k$. Write $f_X(z)=\operatorname{Tr}(XW_z^*)/d$. All spaces are finite dimensional. The norm $\|X\|_2=\sqrt{\operatorname{Tr}(X^*X)}$ is the Hilbert–Schmidt norm, and $\nu_2(\Phi)=\sup_{\rho\ge0,\operatorname{Tr}\rho=1}\|\Phi(\rho)\|_2$ is the maximal output norm. A map in $W_1(H)$ is complex linear, Weyl covariant and satisfies $\Phi(I)=I$; it need not be positive or completely positive. Its computed symbol is $\phi(z)=f_{\Phi(W_z)}(z)$. Put $m(\phi)=\max_{z\ne0}|\phi(z)|^2$ and $E_{\max}(\phi)=\{z\ne0:|\phi(z)|^2=m(\phi)\}$. At $d=1$, explicitly set $m=0$ and $E_{\max}=\varnothing$. Write $S(\phi)=d^{-1/2}\sqrt{1+(d-1)m(\phi)}$.
--
--   The alternating pairing is $[u,v]=u_xv_y-u_yv_x\in\mathbb Z_d$. A subset is degenerate when this pairing vanishes for every pair of its elements. A maximal degenerate subgroup is inclusion maximal among degenerate subsets. For a unit vector $\psi$, define $G_\psi=\{z:\exists c\in\mathbb C,\ W_z\psi=c\psi\}$. Let $G(z)$ be the additive subgroup generated by $z$.
--
--   For $\Phi\in W_1(H)$ the following separate implications hold:
--
--   $$\nu_2(\Phi)=S(\phi)\ \Longrightarrow\ |E_{\max}(\phi)|\ge d-1,$$
--   $$\bigl[\exists\psi,\ \|\psi\|=1,\ |G_\psi|=d,\ G_\psi\setminus\{0\}\subseteq E_{\max}(\phi)\bigr]\ \Longrightarrow\ \nu_2(\Phi)=S(\phi).$$
--
--   There is no contractivity assumption. These are a necessary cardinality condition and a distinct sufficient eigenvector condition, not an equivalence between cardinality and saturation.
-- source:
--   On Weyl-covariant channels, arXiv:quant-ph/0510148v3, PDF p. 6, Theorem 3, necessary and sufficient saturation criteria

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Bridge50_P05

noncomputable section

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Bridge50.P05

open scoped BigOperators Matrix Kronecker ComplexConjugate ComplexOrder ENNReal

open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Information100.P34 (cyclicPhase weyl dephasing)

open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Information100.P08 (IsPure)

open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Gap48.P36 (WeylLabel)

open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Information100.P21 (Op)

open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Information100.P50 (schattenNorm)

open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Claimed50.P48
  (nu superopTensor UniversalMultiplicative rowKraus indexedKrausDilation)

open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Information100.P67 (complementaryChannel)

attribute [local instance] Classical.propDecidable Classical.decEq

variable {d : ℕ} [NeZero d]

/-- Theorem 3, PDF pp.6--7: necessity and sufficiency are separate implications;
the cardinality bound alone is not an iff. No contractivity or CP assumption. -/
theorem saturationCriteria (Phi : Op (ZMod d) →ₗ[ℂ] Op (ZMod d)) (hPhi : NormalizedWeylMap Phi) :
    (nu 2 Phi = saturationValue (symbol Phi) →
      d - 1 ≤ (optimizers (symbol Phi)).ncard) ∧
    ((∃ psi : EuclideanSpace ℂ (ZMod d), ‖psi‖ = 1 ∧
      (eigenSet psi).ncard = d ∧ eigenSet psi \ {0} ⊆ optimizers (symbol Phi)) →
      nu 2 Phi = saturationValue (symbol Phi)) := by sorry

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Bridge50.P05

end
